rows.en:
It was too dark to see clearly, but inside the shoe locker were a pair of eyes, dried out completely.
Not just eyes.
Clean-cut eyebrows, a shapely nose, purple lips...{p}

Shindo was there, strung up from it.
Blood was streaming from his ears and eyes.
He looked like the picture on a tarot card.{p}

His thin back.
If I shoved him away and ran, could I get out of this strange place?
...I'm not so sure I could.{p}

I slowly opened the stall door.
...No one's there.
So Hosoda hasn't been killed?{p}

You actually believe Arai's story?
Well, whatever. Either way, you're going to be killed.
Why, you ask?{p}

Still, where should I go now?
As I walked down the hallway for a while, I suddenly heard Kawahara's voice.
"I see. So that's what you think..."{p}

What had Kawahara wanted me to help him with?
Hashimoto had been so terribly depressed. Maybe he wanted me to be there for her...
He was called a two-faced person, but maybe deep down he was a good person after all.{p}

When I looked at Hashimoto's apology essay, there was a single photograph tucked inside.
Kawahara and Hashimoto were standing side by side in the darkness.
So in the end, Hashimoto did kill herself?{p}In the photo, the two of them were smiling sadly.{p}

No, I can't get near her☆
What's happening?
My head hurts☆{p}
